now metro police have made multiple  arrests in connection to a series of  commercial burglaries in the west part  of the valley christian costas joining  us live in studio with more on what the  suspects were looking for and how they  were able to arrest them bryan metro  police tells us they've made five  arrests within a two-day span thanks to  several leads from the community they  say the suspects were targeting close  businesses that had gaming inside  police say burglaries began in may but  it was the last two incidents on south  fort apache road and del webb boulevard  that helped move the investigation  forward the first happened on via brazil  steakhouse on south fort apache july  10th police say two men smashed the  front door and robbed the slot machines  at the bar  in less than two minutes they left with  three cash boxes the second incident  happened july 21st when two men entered  miller's tavern on del webb boulevard  they left with eight cash boxes police  say they were able to identify a vehicle  which helped locate the suspects  during the colbit and during the  commission of these crimes obviously our  suspects were  wearing masks it was very hard to  identify  but we were able to do that and quickly  police identified sean patrick from  henderson as one of the suspects who  according to reports is a 14-time  convicted felon others named in the  police report are tad massarang and eric  johnson who was driving a stolen vehicle  well police tell us this investigation  is far from over so far only patrick  faces four charges but police tell us  they are waiting for additional charges  to be filed christian casa is 8 news now
 

